- [`install-proxy.sh`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/scripts/deploy/install-proxy.sh:26) rejects only `:latest`; arbitrary mutable tags such as `:prod` pass. Require an exact `@sha256:<64 hex>` reference.
- [`docker-compose.proxy.yml`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/deploy/docker-compose.proxy.yml:7) defaults to the mutable placeholder tag `:pin-me`. Fail when `ASSMUD_PROXY_IMAGE` is absent and require a digest-pinned image.
- [`exportProfilesJson`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/packages/profiles/src/index.ts:58) serializes imported objects unchanged. Because [`importProfilesJson`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/packages/profiles/src/index.ts:62) preserves unknown fields, an imported `proxyToken` or `assmud_token` is re-exported. The new test only tests an unused assertion helper, not the real export path.
- T3 acknowledgment is global and persistent. [`saveCustomWs`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/apps/web/src/lib/trustMode.ts:29) does not invalidate the acknowledgment, so after acknowledging URL A, the user can change to URL B and connect without acknowledging B. Bind acknowledgment to the normalized URL or clear it whenever the URL changes.
- [`canConnect`](/home/cookys/projects/assmud/apps/web/src/lib/trustMode.ts:85) ignores endpoint validity/presence. Self-host/custom mode can enter the connected UI with an empty or invalid URL. Require a valid endpoint; require `wss:` for non-loopback endpoints.

